# Exception to the blanket *.wasm rule above: the known-good TS server
# rollback baseline MUST be tracked. Without it a fresh clone has no way
# back from a bad deploy, and /tmp does not survive a reboot.
# (The many experimental shim builds under shim/build/ stay ignored on
# purpose — they are artifacts, not state.)
!tools/port/ts-server-dll/baseline/*.wasm

# A capture-script artifact: the frame after the spawn attempt. It is
# written with a neutral name on purpose -- the script cannot know
# whether it got a first-person view or the TS main menu, and a file
# named first-person.png holding the menu is a lie.
docs/screenshots/after-spawn.png

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI-generated working docs — kept on this machine, OUT of the repo.
#
# Two reasons, and they are the same reason:
#
#   1. CLUTTER. These are 24 files and ~640 KB of agent-written markdown
#      plus a megabyte of design mocks. Nobody reads them — not a human
#      visitor, not a fresh agent (README, AGENTS, HANDOFF and SPEC are
#      what a new agent reads, and they are all still tracked).
#
#   2. EXPOSURE. The admin console's specs describe the console's
#      endpoints, its auth and lockout rules, and the production host's
#      file paths and ownership. That is reverse-engineering material for
#      a console that can ban players and drive RCON. Same for the
#      production topology's access and hardening sections.
#
# They stay on disk: gitignored, not deleted. `git rm --cached` took
# them out of the repo; the working copies are still here.
#
# NOTE: gitignoring does NOT un-publish. The content is still in this
# repository's git HISTORY, and the repository is public. Anything that
# must actually disappear needs a history rewrite.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/ADMIN-CONSOLE.md
docs/ADMIN-CONSOLE-RUNBOOK.md
docs/ADMIN-CONSOLE-SPEC-DRAFT.md
docs/ADMIN-CONSOLE-UI.md
docs/admin-console-mock.html
docs/screenshots/admin-console-*.png
docs/ASSET-DELIVERY.md
docs/BUY-MENU-UI.md
docs/BUY-MENU-UI-v2.md
docs/cheats/
docs/CLIENT-PERF-RESEARCH.md
docs/CONTROL-PLANE.md
